Package: CYAN
Title: Niche Genomic Analyses — RNA Editing and Variant Calling
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Yohan", "Lefol", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "yohanlefol@proton.me")
Description: Specialised genomic analyses sitting between upstream processing
    (HORIZON) and expression-level analysis (GAIA/CAULDRON). Provides RNA
    editing detection via REDItools2 and somatic variant calling via GATK
    MuTect2. Designed for single-sample workflows with configurable working
    and output directories.
Depends: R (>= 4.3)
Imports:
    basilisk,
    reticulate,
    methods
Suggests:
    VariantAnnotation,
    GenomicRanges,
    BiocManager
SystemRequirements: Python (>= 3.8); GATK >= 4.0 (for MuTect2 functions)
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
biocViews: Sequencing, RNASeq, VariantAnnotation, SNP
Config/roxygen2/version: 8.0.0
